<TEI xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0" xml:id="CH2b1559-en-18cfe757" type="transl"><teiHeader><fileDesc><titleStmt><title>Draft translation of 聲無哀樂論</title><editor role="translator">Christoph Harbsmeier</editor></titleStmt><publicationStmt><ab>published electronically as part of the TLS project at https://hxwd.org</ab><availability status="2"><ab>This work has been licensed for use in the TLS</ab></availability></publicationStmt><sourceDesc><bibl><title>Draft translation of 聲無哀樂論</title>Draft: Oxford, 1971</bibl><ab>Translation of <bibl corresp="#CH2b1559"><title xml:lang="och"/></bibl> into <lang xml:lang="en">English</lang>.</ab></sourceDesc></fileDesc><profileDesc><creation resp="#CH">Initially created: <date>2026-05-10T21:05:56.502+09:00</date> by CH</creation></profileDesc></teiHeader><text><body><div><head>Translated parts</head><p xml:id="CH2b1559-start"><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.59" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-30T22:26:43.692+09:00">1.2.8.1 So then: the Music says this; the Music says that,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.60" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T00:32:04.919+09:00">is there no more to it than bells and drums (and no more)? [Music is more than the bells and drums that express it.]</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.61" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T00:23:53.965+09:00">Grief speaks of this, Grief speaks of that,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.62" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T00:32:53.359+09:00">is there no more to it than wailing and weeping? [Grief is more than its expression in wailing and weeping!</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.63" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T00:36:28.282+09:00">Speaking along these lines</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.64" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-30T15:42:20.349+09:00">jade and silk are not the real substance of ritual (and?) deference,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.65" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T00:44:26.518+09:00">song and dance performance is not the main point of mourning.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.66" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T00:45:06.742+09:00">How is one to make all this plain?</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.67" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T00:46:22.444+09:00">So: different regions have different customs:</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.68" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T00:48:18.979+09:00">their chanting and wailing is not the same.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.69" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T01:02:51.617+09:00">When used in complex contexts</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.70" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T01:03:14.87+09:00">some will hear wailing and feel elated,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.71" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T01:11:02.719+09:00">others will hear singing and feel dejected,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.72" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-30T15:45:12.087+09:00">and yet the essence (itself) of their grief and joy is of the same order.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.73" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-30T22:25:19.254+09:00">1.2.8.2 Now if on the basis of quite the same feelings</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.74" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-30T15:57:31.987+09:00">one emits all sorts of different sounds,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.75" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-30T16:16:05.314+09:00">is this not because the sound is not a constant/stable indicator of emotions?</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.76" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-30T22:25:22.326+09:00">1.2.8.3 And yet the harmonious juxtaposition of musical tones</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.77" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T01:24:49.819+09:00">is what affects humans most profoundly.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.78" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T01:26:39.863+09:00">toiling workers sing songs to their work,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.79" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T01:29:51.532+09:00">those pleased with themselves celebrate their feats through dances.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.80" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T01:31:53.835+09:00">And so those who suffer sad pain in their hearts</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.81" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T01:34:28.541+09:00">will come up with acutely sorrowful words.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.82" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-30T22:25:43.356+09:00">1.2.8.4 Words properly aligned become songs,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.83" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T01:36:11.125+09:00">sounds properly aligned become music:</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.84" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T01:38:11.79+09:00">one mixes these together to intone them,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.85" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T01:38:29.503+09:00">and one gathers to listen to them.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.86" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T01:39:27.144+09:00">The mind gets moved by sounds in harmony,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.87" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-30T16:24:32.458+09:00">and one's emotions is aroused by bitter words:</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.88" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-30T16:24:56.767+09:00">one's sighs never stop,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.89" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-30T16:27:09.098+09:00">one's tears flow freely.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.90" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-30T22:26:03.201+09:00">1.2.8.5 The mourning heart, hidden inside,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.91" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-30T16:33:45.408+09:00">comes into the open only when one meets harmonious musical cadence.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.92" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-30T16:34:27.033+09:00">The harmonious musical cadence is not symbolic of anything,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.93" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-30T16:35:41.961+09:00">whereas the mournful heart has one dominant feature.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.94" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-30T16:36:39.27+09:00">So then, with a mournful heart with this dominant feature</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.95" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-30T16:38:04.185+09:00">on the occasion of a harmonious musical cadence that is not symbolic of anything</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.96" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T01:58:55.731+09:00">what one is struck by</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.97" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T22:18:29.856+09:00">is only mournful grief, that is all:</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.98" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-30T16:42:25.776+09:00">how can one still understand (Zhuang Zhou's) "the blowing  being myriads ways different,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.99" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T22:22:04.793+09:00">and of it causing itself to cease"!</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.100" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-30T22:37:57.243+09:00">1.2.8.6  As customs and manners flow along</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.101" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-30T16:46:37.989+09:00">they end up forming forms of governance,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.102" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-30T16:47:48.732+09:00">and thus the histories of the states elucidate the successes and failures of governance and education,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.103" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-30T16:48:12.728+09:00">investigate the thriving and the decline of the local ways, </seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.104" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-30T16:49:54.897+09:00">they sing the songs of men's natural feelings and their basic nature,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.105" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-30T16:51:04.545+09:00">thus offering critical advice to the authorities.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.106" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-30T16:52:31.899+09:00">Thus we are told (in the 詩序):</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.107" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T23:06:45.233+09:00">"The music of a doomed state is mournful and then wistful."</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-7a.2" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-14T19:34:12.478+09:00">4.2 </seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-9a.77" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-25T21:39:39.916+09:00">making one agitated or serene,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-9a.78" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-25T21:42:07.951+09:00">that is the extrinsic effect of the sounds of music.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-9a.39" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-25T22:29:43.672+09:00">Thus the mind is bound by a host of concerns,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-9a.40" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-25T22:29:49.038+09:00">but the Five Notes are in concert,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-9a.41" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-25T22:32:04.511+09:00">and therefore one feels pleasantly relaxed and satisfied.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-9a.42" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-25T22:33:58.731+09:00">And in this way all the notes are essentially simple, complex, high, low, well executed or badly,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-9a.43" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-25T22:36:48.348+09:00">and the human sensibilities respond with agitation or serenity, concentrated focus or dissolution.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-9a.44" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-25T22:43:43.407+09:00">Just as when you wander about in the markets of the capitals</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-9a.45" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-25T22:48:41.008+09:00">then one's eyes get overexcited and one's urged run wild:  </seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-9a.46" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-25T22:49:21.207+09:00">but when one settles down to observing the measures of music</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-9a.47" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-25T22:50:04.779+09:00">then one's thoughts are serene and one's face is straight.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-9a.48" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-25T22:51:28.237+09:00">This is because the essence of musical melody</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-9a.49" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-25T22:52:35.769+09:00">is all in relaxation and stressfulness.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-9a.50" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-25T22:53:21.908+09:00">The emotional response to musical sound</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-9a.51" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-25T23:14:20.836+09:00">is limited to agitation and serenity."</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.5" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-26T23:09:12.588+09:00">the musical notes of a well-governed age are serene so as to induce joy,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.6" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T04:26:11.869+09:00">and the musical noted of  a doomed age are mournful so as to induce wistfulness. </seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.7" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-26T23:10:15.01+09:00">Now generally, good government and political chaos depend on governance,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.8" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-26T23:14:08.294+09:00">and the sound of the musical notes then reflect (the contrasting kinds of governance).</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.9" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-06-01T00:19:33.429+09:00">【General statement of fact 1.1.2】    So, then, the emotions of grief and wistfulness</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.10" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-26T23:14:34.173+09:00">are expressed by metal and stone (musical instruments),</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.11" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-26T23:14:46.72+09:00">and the abstract feature of of serenity and joy</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.12" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-26T21:19:16.859+09:00">takes shape through wind and string instruments.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.13" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-06-01T00:18:54.702+09:00">【First historical evidence text  1.1.2a】     And there again, when Zhongni came to hear the "Shao" music</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.14" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-26T21:28:05.356+09:00">he recognised in it the virtue of Shun;</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.15" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-06-01T00:18:35.953+09:00">【Second historical evidence text 1.1.2b】 and when Ji Zha listened to the string music</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.16" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-26T21:29:30.301+09:00">he got to understand the customs of all the states.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.17" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-06-01T00:15:01.143+09:00">Assessment of the reliability of the evidence    1.1.3 These are established facts of the past,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.18" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-26T21:36:33.534+09:00">and the great worthies of former times had no doubts about them.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.19" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-06-01T00:18:20.736+09:00">【Address to the Host  1.1.4.1】  Now just you alone have this idea that there is no emotion like grief and joy in the the sounds (of music):</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.20" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-26T22:34:26.827+09:00">Where on earth are your arguments?</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.21" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-06-01T00:21:30.873+09:00">【polite invitation to speak1.1.4.2】 If you have terrific investigations to report</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.22" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-26T22:41:20.15+09:00">please let us have the explanations without delay!</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.23" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-06-01T00:24:19.935+09:00">【Opening general statement on the history of the issue 1.2.1】 The Host responded as follows:</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.24" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-26T22:51:29.103+09:00">"On this issue people have long been stuck:</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.25" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-26T22:55:55.947+09:00">no one has it in him to sort this out.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.26" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-26T22:58:24.064+09:00">That's what got us to the stage, through the ages,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.27" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-26T23:01:36.353+09:00">people have been all wrong about the ins and outs of this.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.28" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-06-01T00:26:13.167+09:00">【Polite general introduction to the intentions of the reply of the host 1.2.2】 So, without delay , having gratefully received your guidance</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.29" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-26T23:53:34.294+09:00">I shall go ahead put in words at least one corner of all this.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.3" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-06-01T00:20:20.133+09:00">【Opening basic questions. 1.1.1.】 There was a Stranger from Qin who consulted the Host of the Eastern Wilds as follows:</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.4" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-26T23:08:22.49+09:00">I'm told that past opinion holds it that</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.30" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-06-01T00:28:37.45+09:00">【The place of sounds of music in cosmology 1.2.2】 So then: When the two vital energies of Heaven and Earth commerge</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.31" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-26T23:55:37.16+09:00">then all manner of creatures get to be born and to grow, </seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.32" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-26T23:58:44.174+09:00">the cold and the hot seasons get to take their turns</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.33" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T00:01:14.778+09:00">and the Five Agents take their full forms.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.34" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T00:05:41.903+09:00">they become visible with the five colours (the world of colours),</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.35" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T00:06:20.189+09:00">and they emit the fives tones (the world of sounds).</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.36" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T00:07:22.952+09:00">The emergence of tones and sounds (of music)</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.37" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T00:13:33.843+09:00">is perhaps like the existence of smells and flavours between Heaven and Earth:</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.38" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-06-01T01:26:59.971+09:00">【Specific conclusion on the unchanging nature of the sounds of music 1.2.2.2】 No matter how excellent or otherwise</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.39" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T00:19:45.115+09:00">and even after they have been exposed to dirty contamination,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.40" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-06-01T01:22:37.081+09:00">their essential substance remains its natural same</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.41" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T00:24:42.29+09:00">and it does not fundamentally change.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.42" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-06-01T01:27:36.185+09:00">How would one change the handling of these things in terms of preference or aversion</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.43" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T00:30:40.554+09:00">and how indeed could emotions like grief and joy change one's objective assessment of these things?</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.44" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-06-01T01:30:50.771+09:00">【On harmony as the crucial relational feature of tones 1.2.3】 That the tones like gong and shang, when gathered and juxtaposed,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.45" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-30T15:04:31.65+09:00">then the musical tones be in striking harmony,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.46" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-30T15:05:16.109+09:00">that is the highest hope for the human mind:</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.47" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-30T15:18:36.756+09:00">This is what one's essential desires are smitten by.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.48" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-06-01T01:33:34.727+09:00">【The background of traditional views on the emotions 1.2.4 】 The ancients were aware that emotions must not be indulgent,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.49" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T00:51:09.647+09:00">that desires must not be extreme,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.50" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-30T08:55:31.521+09:00">and that therefore, as circumstances require,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.51" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-30T08:55:56.73+09:00">one moderates every one of these emotions and desires,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.52" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-30T08:58:15.085+09:00">and one sees to it that grief does not get to the stage of heartbreak,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.53" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T01:00:45.568+09:00">and that joy does not reach the stage of euphoria,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.54" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-06-01T01:34:21.956+09:00">【The logical and conceptual background 1.2.5】 For practical reasons one gives names to things,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.55" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T01:08:42.039+09:00">and so things have their appellations.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.56" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T01:10:47.434+09:00">When someone weeps one diagnoses grief,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.57" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T01:11:05.849+09:00">when someone sings one diagnoses joy.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.108" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-30T22:38:46.687+09:00">1.2.1.8.7 Happiness, anger, mournfulness and joy,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.109" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T04:27:46.35+09:00">love, hatred, shame and fear:</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.110" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-30T16:53:47.729+09:00">quite generally, it is by these eight</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.111" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T04:33:52.813+09:00">that living humans relate to things and transmit their emotions.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.112" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T04:34:07.734+09:00">Each of these eight belongs to its distinct kind</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.113" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T04:36:09.745+09:00">and they must not be confounded.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.114" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-30T16:55:41.281+09:00">??Now, flavours are called (things like) sweet or bitter;??</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.117" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T04:48:35.371+09:00">then the love and hate are properly be predicated me</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.115" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-30T22:39:58.912+09:00">1.2.9.1 If, for example, because X is talented and I like him subjectively,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.116" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T04:46:47.104+09:00">and because B is stupid and I emotionally dislike him,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.118" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T04:55:20.948+09:00">whereas talent and stupidity are properly predicated of A and B (respectively).</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.119" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T17:18:50.616+09:00">For can one, just because one loves a person predicate of him that he is a loving person/loves others?</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.120" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T05:04:00.307+09:00">And can one, just because I hate a person say of him that he "hates others"?</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.121" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T17:12:52.346+09:00">as to something one prefers does one say of this that it "is a preferring taste"?</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.122" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T17:17:58.117+09:00">as for something one finds tastes loathsome: does one say of this that it is "a loathing taste"?</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.123" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-30T22:22:30.694+09:00">1.2.9.2 Talking from this point of view</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.124" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T17:19:52.952+09:00">external manifestation and internal presence are different in their applications,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.125" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T16:47:39.831+09:00">what applies to oneself (like love or hate) and what applies to the other (like talent or stupidity) has different names</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.126" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-30T16:59:02.638+09:00">If the sounds of music are naturally and duly focussed on good or bad quality  </seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.127" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-30T16:59:43.123+09:00">then they no direct link to emotions like grief or joy.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.128" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T16:59:08.384+09:00">If grief and joy naturally and duly emerge only after  emotions are stimulated (by things other than music)</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.129" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T17:01:31.31+09:00">then grief and joy have no direct connection to the the sounds of music.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.130" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T17:21:09.446+09:00">And when both the name and the reality (of these emotions)  are detached (from the sounds of music),  </seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.131" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-30T22:57:08.35+09:00">then the sounds of music can be altogether seen as what they are! ("Mournfulness" and "joyfulness" are properly attributed to persons, not of the sounds of music which are properly said to be "good" or "bad".)</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.132" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-30T22:22:01.913+09:00">1.2.10.1 As for Jizi in Lu</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.133" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T18:36:10.687+09:00">he was picking out Odes and considering rituals</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.134" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T18:37:19.323+09:00">so as to distinguish between the "Airs" and the "Elegantiae":</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.135" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T18:38:28.727+09:00">How could he have decided on their excellence or otherwise just relying on the sounds of the music as such??</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.136" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-30T22:21:57.055+09:00">1.2.10.2 And there again, when Zhongni got to hear the "Shao"</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.137" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T18:44:02.967+09:00">and at its consistency</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.138" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T18:44:26.722+09:00">why, therefore, has his waxing into a sigh</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.139" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T18:48:05.118+09:00">necessarily have to be based on the sound of the music enabling him to understand the virtue of Emperor Shun</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.140" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T18:47:11.763+09:00">before sighing about the beauty (of the Shao)</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.141" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-30T22:21:46.431+09:00">1.2.11 So at this point I've roughly explained one basic point in the matter,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.142" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T22:17:51.589+09:00">but you can surely imagine most of the rest yourself.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-2a.2" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-31T16:34:58.277+09:00">2.1.1.1 The "Stranger from Qin" objected:</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-2a.3" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T22:19:12.409+09:00">Customs vary everywhere in the world</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-2a.5" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T22:21:39.669+09:00">but the emotions of grief and joy,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-2a.6" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T22:21:56.766+09:00">you nowhere fail to find these.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-2a.7" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-31T16:36:03.639+09:00">2.1.1.2 So now when the heart is moved within</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-2a.8" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-31T16:36:48.006+09:00"> the sound/voice comes from the heart.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-2a.9" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T22:24:29.048+09:00">Even if these emotions are given expression in other tones</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-2a.10" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T22:27:20.921+09:00">send forth through other sounds of music,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-2a.11" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-27T22:27:42.806+09:00">those who have ears to hear</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-2a.12" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-31T16:37:16.765+09:00">will be quite naturally alert to this and will make sure they do not get this wrong.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-2a.13" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-31T16:48:50.315+09:00">2.1.2.1a Long ago, wen Bo Ya strummed his lute</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-2a.14" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-31T16:38:57.221+09:00">Zhong Ziqi came to understand what he was driving at;</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-2a.15" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-31T17:24:21.692+09:00">2.1.2.1bwhen the slave (in that story) strikes the musical stones</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-2a.16" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-31T16:40:56.895+09:00">Zichan became aware of the grief in his heart.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-2a.17" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-31T17:24:57.006+09:00">2.1.2.1cWhen the burghers of Lu were found wailing in the mornings</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-2a.18" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-31T16:48:18.681+09:00">Yan Hui concluded that he was nearing the end of his life.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-2a.22" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-31T17:26:41.416+09:00">2.1.2.3</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-2a.27" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-31T17:32:46.47+09:00">2.1.2.4</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-2a.33" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-31T17:33:45.293+09:00">2.1.3.1</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-2a.36" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-31T17:35:05.735+09:00">2.1.3.1.1</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-2a.43" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-31T17:36:39.734+09:00">2.1.3.1.2</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-2a.47" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-31T17:38:17.323+09:00">2.1.4.1a</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-2a.51" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-31T17:39:04.227+09:00">2.1.4.2</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-2a.52" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-31T17:39:34.351+09:00">2.1.4.2a</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-2a.53" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-31T17:39:39.489+09:00">2.1.4.2b</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-2a.54" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-31T17:40:03.572+09:00">2.1.4.2c</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-2a.56" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-31T17:40:46.864+09:00">2.1.4.3</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-2a.61" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-31T17:41:31.4+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-2a.62" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-31T17:42:31.674+09:00">2.1.4.4</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-3a.2" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-31T17:42:42.515+09:00">2.2</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-3a.3" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-31T17:43:08.67+09:00">2.2.1</seg></p></div></body></text></TEI>